/**
 * Every Columbia course the bulletin publishes a description for.
 *
 * Generated by `python3 ingest/emit-catalog.py` from the pages committed under
 * `data/snapshots/courses/`, one file per course, fetched from the university's
 * own bulletin. Do not edit by hand: rerun the script.
 *
 * These carry `verified: false`, which is not a formality. The prerequisite
 * trees were parsed from the bulletin's own grammar rather than read by a
 * person, so the UI shows an "ask your advisor" note against anything the
 * parser could not turn into a course id, and against any prerequisite naming a
 * course this catalog does not hold. The hand-checked courses in `columbia.ts`
 * carry `verified: true` and take precedence over anything here.
 *
 * The skill tags are a no-API-key fallback. With a key, relevance reads these
 * same descriptions against the actual posting and quotes the proving sentence,
 * which is strictly better. Either way the evidence comes from the catalog.
 */
